  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "2v2 with corner jokers",
  "description": "Play 2v2 at one goal with a goalkeeper, on half a court. In each corner of the area stands a passing joker (J) – four in all. The jokers always play with the team that has the ball and try to move it on first time. Both teams attack the same goal.\n\nUse the jokers to build quick combinations: pass, move straight away and get the ball back in a more dangerous spot. Wall passes with the jokers shift the defenders and open routes to a shot. A team that wins the ball must play through a joker before it may score – this pushes the players to attack through passing instead of running straight at goal.\n\nSwap court players and jokers after a few minutes. In the picture the jokers are blue with a J, but they do not belong to either team. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass and move – go straight after your pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Get open for the joker in a spot where you can shoot first time."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Use the overload: with the jokers you always outnumber the defenders."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Jokers: play first time and look up before the ball arrives."
    }
  ],
